= Assembly Reconvenes

After the break cut short by Staal's insistence, the Assembly is back in session. Reportedly, Staal has obtained DuFour's authorization for an unconstitutional decree, presumably in the vein of forcing the Assembly's adjournment or cancelling new elections.

However, the situation has changed, Staal is much more popular and its expected that the backlash to an unconstitutional act will be more limited, and not be to the degree that it would provoke a civil war. 

- @reichstag

@reichstag
title: The Assembly enters session.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pro_republic -= 20;

Q.staal_marcher_r -= 2;
Q.staal_marcher_influence -= 1;
Q.staal_marcher_support -= 3;

Q.commons_collectivist -= 6;
Q.burgher_collectivist -= 2;
Q.disfavored_collectivist -= 6;

Q.commons_marcher -= 2;
Q.burgher_marcher -= 2;
Q.disfavored_marcher -= 2;

Q.commons_gnu += 6;
Q.burgher_gnu += 4;
Q.disfavored_gnu += 4;

Q.commons_gnu_bonus += 6;
Q.burgher_gnu_bonus += 4;
Q.disfavored_gnu_bonus += 4;

Q.rfb_militancy *= 0.6;
Q.rfb_strength *= 0.6;
Q.rb_militancy *= 0.95;
Q.rb_strength *= 0.95;

Q.reichstag_rubicon = 0;
Q.reichstag_break = 1;
Q.reichstag_joever = 1;

Q.next_reichstag_time = Q.rubicon_time + 10000;
Q.next_reichstag_week = Q.week;
Q.next_reichstag_month = Q.month + 12;
Q.next_reichstag_year = Q.year;

if (Q.next_reichstag_week > 4) {
  Q.next_reichstag_week -= 4;
  Q.next_reichstag_month += 1;
}

if (Q.next_reichstag_week > 4) {
  Q.next_reichstag_week -= 4;
  Q.next_reichstag_month += 1;
}

if (Q.next_reichstag_month > 12) {
  Q.next_reichstag_month -= 12;
  Q.next_reichstag_year += 1;
}
!}

Staal immediately issues his decree to unconstitutionally adjourn the Assembly indefinitely, declaring that the chamber will remain closed until the parties prove they can govern constructively again. Reactions inside the chamber are mixed: Staal's supporters applaud the chancellor’s show of strong leadership, while the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span> ignite brawls that police are forced to break up.

In the following days, civil demonstrations are violently suppressed. Police disperse crowds with tear gas, street clashes erupt, and several civilians are killed. The strengthened Commonwealth Army and the divided stance of <span style="color: #000000;">repu</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">bli</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">cans</span> make any serious rebellion futile. At least half of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communist**</span> deputies in the Assembly are arrested and sent to special courts for inciting violence.

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> remains largely untouched[? if rb_militancy > 0.1:, though suspicious activity has been reported to be planned against the the Banners?].